flow=[('01','Find the intention','Describe who the product is for and the experience it should support. A sketch, conversation or existing object can be enough to begin.','A brief that another person can understand.'),('02','Make and learn','Prepare a sample. Try it in the real setting. Keep observations about fit, flavour, comfort, use and care attached to the version tested.','A sample record and a clear next revision.'),('03','Connect the means','Bring together materials, artwork, makers and quotations. Compare the same specification, quantities and delivery terms.','An agreed specification, contributions and dated costs.'),('04','Shape the offer','Explain exactly what someone receives, the price, variants, timing and handover. Keep a single item, a refill and a collection as distinct offers.','An understandable offer and a fulfilment plan.'),('05','Share the experience','Use the product, tell its story and invite feedback. People choose their participation, and creators agree how their work is used.','Release material, customer questions and useful feedback.'),('06','Follow the next use','Record repairs, returns, refills and recovery with a real receiving route. Bring costs, losses and experience into the next design.','A completed movement and learning for the next cycle.')]
steps=''.join(f'<article class="step" id="step-{i}"><span>{i}</span><div><h2>{t}</h2><p>{d}</p><p><strong>What comes out:</strong> {o}</p></div></article>' for i,t,d,o in flow)
add('how-it-works.html','How the engine works','Follow an idea through samples, agreements, offers, participation and continued use.',head('A connected way<br>to make things happen.','An idea does not move in a straight line. A sample changes the brief. A customer changes the offer. A return improves the next design.')+f'''<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="split"><div><h2>Start wherever<br>the opportunity is.</h2><p>A maker can start with spare capacity. A community can start with a shared need. Someone else can start with a material looking for a new use.</p><p>The steps below are a useful route through the work. They are not ranks, gates controlled by a central authority, or a compulsory sequence.</p></div><div class="note"><h3>Agree the work, together.</h3><p>Record the contribution, the people involved, its terms and its limits. A responsibility lasts for the agreed activity. It does not become permanent standing over others.</p></div></div></div></section><img class="full-photo" src="assets/process.png" alt="Concept product studio linking purple textile samples, a botanical drink and a reusable bottle with a gold thread" loading="lazy" width="1536" height="1024"><div class="hero-caption">AI-generated concept artwork. Samples and connected making.</div><section class="section"><div class="wrap prose"><div class="steps">{steps}</div>{source('chapters 1, 2 and 10 to 16')}</div></section><section class="section green"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>One record.<br>Many useful views.</h2><p>A product connects with its material, pattern, maker, offer and feedback. A project can connect to several products. There is no required parent project.</p></div><div><p>A revised fabric should reach the maker’s brief, costs and product description. The working edition lets you keep that information together and export a portable pack.</p><p>Live synchronisation between businesses, stock systems and AI services is part of the wider design.</p></div></div></section>''')

cases=[
('aura-undies','Aura Undies','A value chosen by the wearer.','Comfortable underwear and related garments carrying a personally chosen word such as love, courage, kindness, joy or peace. The maker’s identity stays discreet.','Compare fabric feel, cut, support, seams, size and word placement. Keep wear and wash feedback with each garment version.','Everyday pairs, multipacks and more luxurious fabrics are possible offers. Record the actual variant, maker and quotation.','Durability and accurate sizing come first. Record the acceptance conditions of a suitable textile recovery service for worn intimate garments.','4'),
('aura-expressions','Aura of expressions','Personal meaning, with room to grow.','Love, Health, Joy, Peace, Intimacy, Virtue, Courage, Curiosity, Beauty and Inspiration are creative starting points. People can add expressions, languages and interpretations.','Explore the chosen expression through a useful object: a journal, mug, bag, eye mask, print, garment or gift. Fluent speakers review wording in their language.','Give each object its own offer. A collection can bring music, a drink or a journal together around an experience.','Choose durable formats and care instructions. Meaning is personal; an expression does not promise a health or psychological result.','3'),
('drinks','Drinks and elixirs','Flavour, preparation and shared moments.','Botanical infusions, tea blends, ready-to-drink beverages and concentrates offer different ways to create an enjoyable ritual.','Record recipe versions, ingredients, quantities, serving format and maker-confirmed storage requirements. Gather feedback on flavour, aroma, texture and convenience.','A single serving, household concentrate and hospitality pack have different costs, packaging and delivery needs.','A refill needs a receiving point, suitable container, cleaning process and cost. The name “elixir” is a creative description, not a claim of treatment.','5'),
('p4a','P4A merchandise','Purple identity, practical objects.','Start with purple hoodies, shirts, stickers, homewares and event material connected to the P4A project.','Agree artwork use and test fit, colour, fabric and print finish before a production run.','Separate the item price, delivery and any voluntary support amount. The plan describes the existing gear checkout as a test that takes no payment.','Use care, repairs and suitable recovery to extend garment life. Links to the project explain the collection’s own story.','6'),
('gajra','GAJRA Earth merchandise','An everyday expression of abundance.','Create a collection around Joyful Responsible Abundance, using clothing, bottles, mugs, bags, journals, prints or other useful formats.','Choose the object first, develop suitable artwork, agree its use and prepare the production files.','Name the maker, materials, price and fulfilment arrangement. State any contribution to associated work for the particular offer.','Share capable makers and production methods with other collections while retaining the collection’s identity and agreements.','6'),
('hygiene','Hygiene and care','Useful routines, carefully specified.','Explore soap, wash products, cleaning cloths and bathroom accessories through the real setting in which someone uses them.','Define body or surface contact, material, cleaning method, packaging and continued-use cost. Product performance needs evidence from the actual construction or formulation.','Keep care information, supported claims and supply arrangements with the product version.','Reusable cloths and refill formats need suitable handling and receiving arrangements, with their operating cost included.','7'),
('purple-mat','The purple piss mat','A recognisable joke. A useful bathroom object.','A named P4A concept that brings purple identity and toilet humour into a practical mat. Its precise placement and construction remain design choices.','Test dimensions, absorbency, backing, floor stability, drying, odour, colourfastness and repeated cleaning. Any scent or treatment needs its own specification.','Show the real object, dimensions, materials, price, care and delivery once developed. The concept illustration is not a tested product.','Follow the selected construction through washing, replacement parts and an actual material receiving route.','7'),
('sandy-club','Sandy Sports and Screen Club','A club collection, shaped by its participants.','The plan’s worked example connects sand sports and screen gatherings with shirts, hoodies, hats, bottles, bags and event prints.','The club chooses its identity, artwork, products, contributors, ordering window and production quantities. Other clubs begin with their own choices.','Explain price, timing, minimum batch, collection or delivery and any contribution to club activity. State what happens if the minimum is missed.','Reorders reuse the agreed specification. Repair, suitable second-hand exchange and sharing can extend useful life. A mutual for shared purchasing is optional.','8'),
('joy-gathering','An Aura of Joy gathering','One complete cycle to explore.','Bring an elixir recipe, original music and reusable serving items into a shared brief. Participants agree the experience and their contributions.','Make and taste samples, develop a label, agree creative use and prepare a demonstration. The people involved choose what is published.','Connect the event invitation, product offers, orders and practical serving arrangements. Guests choose whether to buy, give feedback or join another activity.','Record containers returned, stock remaining, losses, receipts and agreed payments. Use that experience to shape the next gathering.','18')]
product_cards=''.join(f'<a class="card card-link" href="#{slug}"><h3>{title}</h3><p>{tagline}</p></a>' for slug,title,tagline,*rest in cases)
details=''
for slug,title,tagline,intro,make,offer,circular,chapter in cases:
    action=f'<a class="btn" href="workbench.html?case={slug}">Explore this case ↗</a>' if args.stage>=3 else '<a class="inline-link" href="sources/JRA-Product-Engine-Plan.pdf">Read the full source plan</a>'
    details+=f'<article class="section" id="{slug}"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><h2>{title}</h2><p>{tagline}</p></div><p class="lead">{intro}</p><div class="cards"><div class="card"><h3>Make and test</h3><p>{make}</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Shape the offer</h3><p>{offer}</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Continue the use</h3><p>{circular}</p></div></div><div class="actions" style="margin-top:30px">{action}</div>{source("chapter "+chapter)}</div></article>'
add('products.html','Product case studies','Explore all the plan’s starting ideas, from Aura Undies and drinks to P4A, GAJRA Earth and club collections.',head('Many starting points.<br>Yours to explore.','The plan’s product ideas are here as case studies you can open, adapt and connect. They offer starting material while leaving decisions with the people doing the work.')+f'<section class="section tint"><div class="wrap"><p class="note">These are concepts and planning examples. They are not stock listings, confirmed partnerships or products available to buy here.</p><div class="cards">{product_cards}</div></div></section>'+details)
